B=r'''<style>.box p,.box li{font-size:19.5px;line-height:1.25}.box h2{font-size:23px;margin-bottom:4px}.tbl{font-size:17.5px}.note,.warn{font-size:17px}.tbl th,.tbl td{padding:2px 6px}.iq ol{font-size:19px;line-height:1.26}.pill{font-size:16px}.grid{gap:10px}.handle{bottom:-12px}.box{padding:9px 12px}.tagline{font-size:19px;margin-bottom:9px}.code{font-family:Consolas,'DejaVu Sans Mono',monospace;background:#f1f5f9;border:1px dashed #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:5px 7px;margin:4px 0;line-height:1.3;font-size:15.5px}</style>
<div class="title">⚡ HxGN EAM Compatible Units <span class="badge">CHEAT SHEET</span></div>
<div class="tagline">Estimate utility projects from standard building blocks, then push the approved estimate straight into a work order. (Infor EAM 11.7 brief)</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="box c1"><h2>1. Key terms</h2><ul><li><b>CU Library record</b>: template of labor, parts, tools, services (+ Child CUs)</li><li><b>CU Design Project</b>: project flagged for CUs; many estimates</li><li><b>CU Estimate</b>: work points + CUs → total cost</li><li><b>Work Point</b> / <b>Span</b> (a length, e.g. a trench)</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c2"><h2>2. Setup before use</h2><ul><li>Screen Designer: show <b>Available for CUs</b> (Trades, Tools, Parts, Departments)</li><li>Show <b>CU Standard Rate / Price</b> fields</li><li>System Codes: CUAJ adjustments L0–L9, M0–M9, T0–T9</li><li>Activity Type codes (ACTP)</li><li>Status authorizations for PROJ, CUES, CULB (delivered for R5)</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c3"><h2>3. Org Options</h2><table class="tbl"><tr><th>Option</th><th>Controls</th></tr><tr><td>CUESFERC</td><td>Generate FERC Unit Estimate</td></tr><tr><td>CUESOVHD</td><td>Apply overhead codes</td></tr><tr><td>CUESREMV</td><td>Remove labor % of Install</td></tr><tr><td>CUESTRFR</td><td>Transfer labor % of Install</td></tr><tr><td>CUESSPMT</td><td>Span overage % for length parts</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="box c4"><h2>4. Four estimate types</h2><table class="tbl"><tr><th>Type</th><th>Use</th></tr><tr><td>Cost Only</td><td>Cost estimate only</td></tr><tr><td><b>Design</b></td><td>Cost + Generate WO Activities</td></tr><tr><td>As-Built</td><td>True-up actuals (cost only)</td></tr><tr><td>Template</td><td>Copy into Design estimates</td></tr></table><div class="note">Since 11.7 the CU Design WO sits on the estimate, not the project.</div></div>
<div class="box c5"><h2>5. Action Type selection</h2><ul><li>Actions: <b>Install, Remove, Abandon, Transfer</b></li><li>Only lines with the <b>same</b> action are costed</li><li>Blank action: labor/tools/services count for any action</li><li>Parts need an <b>exact</b> action match</li><li>Adjustment fields must match too (or be blank)</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c6"><h2>6. Estimate status (CUES)</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:4px"><span class="pill">Not Estimated</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Estimated</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Quoted</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Approved</span></div><ul><li>After Not Estimated, Work Points / Suppliers / CU tabs are <b>protected</b></li><li>To edit: set back to Not Estimated, re-estimate</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c7"><h2>7. Worked example (Install)</h2><div class="code">Pole assembly = Pole + 2 Crossarm + Transformer<br>Labor 6 h × $40      = $240<br>Parts 500+2×200+1000 = $1,900<br>Tools 1.5 h × $100   = $150<br>Total                = $2,290</div><div class="note">Brief's example uses CU standard rates/prices.</div></div>
<div class="box c8"><h2>8. Generate WO Activities</h2><ul><li>Only <b>Design</b> type in <b>Approved</b> status</li><li>Deletes existing deletable activities first</li><li>One activity per CU; creates Plan Labor, Parts, Plan Tools + material list</li><li>Services → <b>hired labor</b> lines</li><li>Same Activity Type → merged into one activity</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c1" style="grid-column:1 / span 2"><h2>9. Costing add-ons</h2><table class="tbl"><tr><th>Screen</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td><b>CU Accounting Codes</b></td><td>Accounting Code + Regulatory Account (e.g. POLES → FERC 364); optional CapEx flag</td></tr><tr><td><b>CU Fixed Asset Codes</b></td><td>Finer level inside an accounting code; feed the FERC Unit Estimate tab</td></tr><tr><td><b>CU Overhead Codes</b></td><td>Apply To Labor / Parts-Stock / Parts-Non-stock / Services / Tools; factor 10 = 10% surcharge; Overhead Type (OVTP) e.g. Government vs Private</td></tr><tr><td><b>Copy CU Estimate</b></td><td>Template → Design, or Design → As-Built</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="bottom">
<div class="box" style="border-color:#1a5f7a"><h2 style="color:#1a5f7a">10a. Estimator flow</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:4px"><span class="pill">CU Library</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">CU Design Project</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">CU Estimate + Work Points</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Perform Estimation</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Quote / Approve</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Generate WO Activities</span></div></div>
<div class="box iq"><h2>10b. Consultant tips</h2><ol><li>Give every part line an action</li><li>Set CU rates before estimating</li><li>Use Activity Type to group work</li><li>Keep a Template per job type</li></ol></div>
<div class="box" style="border-color:#2d8a5a"><h2 style="color:#2d8a5a">10c. Key points</h2><ul><li>Same job, same estimate</li><li>Design to WO in one click</li><li>FERC-ready cost split</li></ul></div>
</div></div>'''
build("/workspace/instagram-assets/posts/2026-10-29-linkedin-eam-compatible-units",B,1620,"Rahul Kumar")
